  "notes": "FORMS:\n{混|こん} (mix) + {和|わ} (harmonize, blend). Implies mixing things together into a harmonious blend.\n\nUSAGE:\nA technical term more common in scientific, pharmaceutical, and industrial contexts than in everyday conversation. For everyday mixing, {混|ま}ぜる is more natural.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {混合|こんごう}: mixing, mixture (more general)\n- {混|ま}ぜる: to mix (everyday verb)\n- {調合|ちょうごう}: compounding, preparation (especially medicine)\n- {配合|はいごう}: blending, formulation\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {混和|こんわ}{材|ざい}: admixture (concrete additive)\n- {混和|こんわ}{剤|ざい}: blending agent",
